Subject: [PATCH] mtk: cpuidle: cancel the prediction timer on governor disable

gov_disable_device() can return while other CPUs still use MHSP. Cancel
this instance's timer before that return, not only when the final CPU
disables the governor. Otherwise it can cause a stale timer wakeup or
race with the memset and hrtimer_init on a later enable.

Use synchronous cancellation so an in-flight callback finishes before the
instance can be reinitialized. The callback takes no governor-disable lock.
Do not change active-governor timer deadlines or wake-source handling.
This targets the MHSP vendor module, not the common kernel boot image.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/governors/MHSP/lpm-mhsp.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/governors/MHSP/lpm-mhsp.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/governors/MHSP/lpm-mhsp.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/lpm/governors/MHSP/lpm-mhsp.c
@@ -753,6 +753,7 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	gov->enable = false;
+	hrtimer_cancel(&gov->shallow.histtimer);
 	for_each_possible_cpu(cpu) {
 		struct gov_info *gov = &per_cpu(gov_infos, cpu);
 
